From b2e3f0dd922f862bc7a5ade1e4098f8b300b05c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Ryan X. Charles" <ryan@ryanxcharles.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:26:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add Astrohacker Red fork guidance

Red joins the forks with rules in tow;
Its patches tell us where to go.
---
 AGENTS.md | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index cfe3344..b393446 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -1,18 +1,37 @@
-# Pull Requests
+# AGENTS.md — Red fork for RedVim
 
-Before creating, editing, or marking a PR ready, read and follow
-`.agents/skills/good-pr/SKILL.md`.
+This is Astrohacker's ignored product fork of `codersauce/red`, the source
+baseline for RedVim. The executable is still upstream `red` 0.7.0; RedVim
+branding, bundled Nushell highlighting and publication are not implemented.
 
-The `good-pr` instructions override generic GitHub/PR publishing defaults.
-Do not open draft PRs unless the user explicitly asks for a draft, and do not
-add title prefixes such as `[codex]` unless requested.
+Astrohacker repository guidance and the issues-and-experiments workflow govern
+this checkout. Read the monorepo's `patches/AGENTS.md`, `patches/red/AGENTS.md`
+and `patches/red/README.md` before changes. Use branches named
+`issue-{ISSUE_ID}-exp{N}-{slug}`. Every intentional fork commit, including this
+overlay, needs an ordered format-patch archive, reconstruction pin and manifest
+update in the same experiment result. Never leave source changes local-only.
+Keep this file identical in the fork commit and the monorepo-tracked overlay.
 
-# New Features
+Preserve upstream history, attribution, LICENSE and dependency notices. Do not
+add this nested repository, binaries or build caches to the monorepo index.
+Keep RedVim independent of TermSurf and NuTorch release inputs. Do not install
+an `rvim` command; it conflicts with Vim's restricted mode.
 
-Unless strictly asked, create new features on new worktrees using the worktrunk
-tool with the wt command.
+Run Cargo inside this fork's workspace, not the monorepo workspace:
 
-# Validation
+```nu
+cd forks/red
+cargo build --locked --release --bin red
+./target/release/red --version
+./target/release/red --help
+```
 
-Run `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` before pushing
-Rust changes, and fix every warning or error it reports.
+Use a Rust toolchain supporting the workspace's Rust 2024 crates and native
+C/C++ build tools for bundled parsers. Reuse Cargo caches. Do not remove or
+regenerate the upstream lockfile to bypass a failed locked build.
+
+Upstream validation guidance: before pushing Rust changes, run
+`cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings` and resolve findings.
+For an explicitly requested upstream PR, also read upstream's
+`.agents/skills/good-pr/SKILL.md`. Astrohacker branch/worktree and review policy
+supersedes upstream's automatic worktrunk/new-worktree instructions.
-- 
